<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.20.xsd">

  <!--
      Session-member liveness — the column the ghost-member reaper reads.

      Until now `session_members.left_at` was stamped ONLY by an explicit
      `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}/me` or by `ModerationService.kickPlayer`.
      A tab close, a browser crash, a closed laptop lid or a dropped
      network left the row active forever: the player kept a seat and an
      avatar slot against the room's 16-player cap with nothing left alive
      to release it.

      `last_seen_at` records the most recent liveness signal the BFF saw
      from that member. Two signals feed it, and they are the only two an
      *identified* member produces:

        1. `GET /api/sessions/{id}` — the roster poll. Fires whether or not
           the player is touching anything, which is what makes it safe to
           reap on. It comes from the ANGULAR HOST SHELL
           (`SessionHeartbeatService`, every 20 s while a tab holds a seat),
           because the shell owns the session for every game.
           `shadows-of-the-net` additionally polls from inside the game
           (`session_bridge.gd ROSTER_POLL_INTERVAL`, 5 s) — that is one
           title's own behaviour, not a property of the platform. No other
           game in `games/` calls `/api/sessions/` at all, so a reaper built
           on the game-side poll alone would collect two players halfway
           through a game of chess.
        2. `POST /api/controls/{cid}` / `POST /api/input/{cid}` carrying
           `X-Session-Id` — both funnel through
           `GameSessionService.authorizeControl`, one chokepoint over every
           game's hot path. Player-action-driven, so it is a supplement to
           the poll and never a substitute for it: on a turn-based board
           both players are idle while one of them thinks.

      Deliberately NOT derived from player position: `GameStateService
      .applyControl` only maps MOVE_*/JUMP, so every `SOTN_*` action falls
      to `default -> before` and never reaches `persistPosition` →
      `PositionCacheService.markPresent`. A position-derived heartbeat sees
      zero Shadows-of-the-Net players.

      Nullable rather than NOT NULL so the backfill below and the reaper's
      COALESCE(last_seen_at, joined_at) both stay correct for rows written
      by any code path that predates this column.
  -->

  <!--
      Deliberately NO column DEFAULT. Postgres fills every EXISTING row with
      the default at ADD COLUMN time (the value is stored in the table's
      metadata and read back for all pre-existing rows), so a
      `defaultValueComputed="CURRENT_TIMESTAMP"` here would leave zero NULLs
      behind and turn 061-2's backfill into a no-op — handing every ghost that
      accumulated before this migration a fresh grace window from the very
      changeset meant to collect them.

      Nothing needs the default: `GameSessionService.newMember` seeds
      last_seen_at on the only INSERT path there is, and the reaper reads
      COALESCE(last_seen_at, joined_at) so a row from any path that forgets
      still resolves to an honest instant rather than to "never stale".
  -->
  <changeSet id="061-1-session-members-last-seen-at" author="nin">
    <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
      <not><columnExists tableName="session_members" columnName="last_seen_at"/></not>
    </preConditions>
    <addColumn tableName="session_members">
      <column name="last_seen_at" type="timestamp with time zone"/>
    </addColumn>
  </changeSet>

  <!--
      Backfill existing rows off joined_at rather than NOW(): an already-
      ghosted row must NOT be handed a fresh 90 s of grace by the very
      migration that introduces the reaper. Joining is itself a liveness
      signal, so joined_at is the honest lower bound, and every genuinely
      dead row is immediately past the cutoff on the first sweep.
  -->
  <changeSet id="061-2-backfill-last-seen-at" author="nin">
    <sql>
      UPDATE session_members
         SET last_seen_at = joined_at
       WHERE last_seen_at IS NULL;
    </sql>
  </changeSet>

  <!--
      The reaper's query is "active members, oldest liveness first". The
      partial index keeps it off a full scan as the membership ledger grows
      (rows are append-only — departed members are never deleted).
  -->
  <changeSet id="061-3-index-active-last-seen" author="nin">
    <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
      <not><indexExists indexName="ix_session_members_active_last_seen"/></not>
    </preConditions>
    <sql>
      CREATE INDEX ix_session_members_active_last_seen
      ON session_members (last_seen_at)
      WHERE left_at IS NULL;
    </sql>
  </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
